    {
      "id": "a2.g02.l2", "title": "Irregular participles: daily life", "kind": "grammar",
      "explain": [
        { "type": "p", "text": "Many common verbs have an **irregular participle**. You cannot predict it from the stem, so learn each one together with the infinitive. Most end in **-en** (*gegeten*), some are short (*gedaan, gehad*), and a few end in **-d** or **-t** (*gezegd, gedacht*)." },
        { "type": "table", "head": ["infinitive", "participle", "infinitive", "participle"], "rows": [["eten", "gegeten", "lezen", "gelezen"], ["drinken", "gedronken", "schrijven", "geschreven"], ["zien", "gezien", "nemen", "genomen"], ["doen", "gedaan", "geven", "gegeven"], ["hebben", "gehad", "helpen", "geholpen"], ["slapen", "geslapen", "spreken", "gesproken"], ["zitten", "gezeten", "kijken", "gekeken"]] },
        { "type": "ex", "nl": "Wij hebben pizza gegeten en cola gedronken.", "en": "We ate pizza and drank cola." },
        { "type": "ex", "nl": "Heb je goed geslapen?", "en": "Did you sleep well?" },
        { "type": "tip", "text": "These verbs all use **hebben**. Learn the participle as a pair: *eten – gegeten*. Your lexicon shows the forms of every verb." }
      ],
      "items": [
        { "type": "choice", "q": "Wij hebben pizza ___. (eten)", "options": ["gegeten", "geeten", "gegeeten"], "answer": 0 },
        { "type": "choice", "q": "Ik heb een brief ___. (schrijven)", "options": ["geschreven", "geschreef", "geschrijfd"], "answer": 0 },
        { "type": "choice", "q": "Participle of zitten?", "options": ["gezeten", "gezit", "gezitten"], "answer": 0 },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Ik heb koffie ___. (drinken)", "answers": ["gedronken"], "en": "I drank coffee." },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Heb je die film ___? (zien)", "answers": ["gezien"], "en": "Have you seen that film?" },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Wat heb je gisteren ___? (doen)", "answers": ["gedaan"], "en": "What did you do yesterday?" },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Zij heeft de hele nacht ___. (slapen)", "answers": ["geslapen"], "en": "She slept all night." },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Hij heeft de krant ___. (lezen)", "answers": ["gelezen"], "en": "He read the newspaper." },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Mijn buurman heeft mij ___. (helpen)", "answers": ["geholpen"], "en": "My neighbour helped me." },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Wij hebben lang op het terras ___. (zitten)", "answers": ["gezeten"], "en": "We sat on the terrace for a long time." },
        { "type": "gap", "text": "Ik heb vandaag geen tijd ___. (hebben)", "answers": ["gehad"], "en": "I had no time today." },
        { "type": "transform", "q": "Ik eet een broodje.", "instruction": "Make it perfect tense", "answers": ["Ik heb een broodje gegeten"] },
        { "type": "transform", "q": "Zij leest een boek.", "instruction": "Make it perfect tense", "answers": ["Zij heeft een boek gelezen", "Ze heeft een boek gelezen"] },
        { "type": "transform", "q": "Wij zien Anna.", "instruction": "Make it perfect tense", "answers": ["Wij hebben Anna gezien", "We hebben Anna gezien"] },
        { "type": "order", "answer": "Ik heb gisteren een brief geschreven.", "alt": ["Gisteren heb ik een brief geschreven."], "en": "Yesterday I wrote a letter." },
        { "type": "order", "answer": "Heb je goed geslapen?", "en": "Did you sleep well?" },
        { "type": "translate", "en": "I drank a lot of water.", "answers": ["Ik heb veel water gedronken"] },
        { "type": "translate", "en": "Did you see Tom?", "answers": ["Heb je Tom gezien", "Heb jij Tom gezien", "Hebt u Tom gezien", "Heeft u Tom gezien"] },
        { "type": "match", "pairs": [["eten", "gegeten"], ["nemen", "genomen"], ["geven", "gegeven"], ["spreken", "gesproken"]] }
      ],
